{# FILES · STORAGE — where the bytes actually are, what was bought and how
   much is left.

   IT READS; the targets are edited on the configure page's Storage targets
   section. It exists because "how full is it" is a daily question and a
   settings page is not where a daily question is answered.

   A TARGET WITH NO QUOTA TYPED DRAWS NO BAR rather than a full one: an
   unmeasured share and a full one are different facts.

   A LIST TAB, SO NO STRIP: the section's figures are the Overview's. #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiStorage/base.html.twig' %}
{% import '@UhifadhiStorage/files/_table.html.twig' as tbl %}

{% block title %}Files — Storage{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}<a href="/">uhifadhi</a> / files / storage{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Files{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}Where the bytes actually are, what was bought and how much is left.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}
    <a class="tgl w-act" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Controller\\FilesController::SETTINGS')) }}">{{ ux_icon('storage:settings') }} Where files go</a>
{% endblock %}

{% block storage_page %}
    {% set here = constant('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Controller\\FilesSectionController::STORAGE') %}
    {% set base = filter|filter((v, k) => k not in ['role', 'page']) %}
    {% set options = [{label: 'all', count: all|length, query: base, on: filter.role is not defined}] %}
    {% for role, count in roles %}
        {% set options = options|merge([{label: role, count: count, query: base|merge({role: role}), on: (filter.role ?? null) == role}]) %}
    {% endfor %}

    <div class="c" style="margin-bottom:20px">
        <span class="tab">Where the bytes are<span class="src">&middot; {{ all|length }} {{ all|length == 1 ? 'target' : 'targets' }} &middot; read-only here</span></span>
        <div class="sxlead">
            <span class="t">{{ ux_icon('storage:lock') }}<span><b>Originals live outside the website.</b> No address anybody can guess or share &middot; answered only after a permission check.</span></span>
            <span class="a"><a class="tgl" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Controller\\FilesController::SETTINGS')) }}">Configure storage</a></span>
        </div>
        {{ tbl.bar(here, filter, tbl.chip(here, 'target', 'Filter by target', options), 'Find a storage') }}
        <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr><th>Target</th><th class="num">Files</th><th class="num">Used</th><th class="num">Bought</th><th>Filled</th><th class="num"></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
            {% for row in rows %}
                <tr>
                    <td><b>{{ row.place.label }}</b> <span class="chip{{ row.place.current ? ' ok' }}">{{ row.place.current ? 'default' : row.place.kind }}</span><div class="mono d" style="font-size:10.5px;margin-top:4px">{{ row.place.what }}{% if row.place.where %} &middot; {{ row.place.where }}{% endif %}</div></td>
                    <td class="num">{{ row.files|number_format }}</td>
                    <td class="num">{{ row.bytes|storage_bytes }}</td>
                    <td class="num">{{ row.quotaBytes is null ? '&mdash;'|raw : row.quotaBytes|storage_bytes }}</td>
                    {# NO QUOTA TYPED, NO BAR. Drawing an empty one would claim
                       a measurement nobody made. #}
                    <td>{% if row.filled is not null %}<span class="sxbar" style="display:grid"><span class="t"><i class="f" style="width:{{ min(row.filled, 100) }}%"></i></span></span>{% else %}<span class="mono d">not measured</span>{% endif %}</td>
                    <td class="num">{{ row.filled is null ? '&mdash;'|raw : row.filled ~ ' %' }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% else %}
                <tr><td colspan="6"><span class="mono d">{{ all is empty ? 'No storage is configured, so nothing can be written.' : 'No storage matches these filters.' }}</span></td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {{ include('@Shell/_foot.html.twig', {
            count: table.total, noun: 'storages', one: 'storage',
            perPage: table.size, page: table.page, pages: table.pages, links: links,
        }, with_context: false) }}
        <div class="sxfoot">
            <span>Switching the target asks whether to move what is already kept &middot; the answer decides</span>
            <span class="sp"></span>
            <a class="tgl" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Controller\\FilesController::SETTINGS')) }}">Where files go</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2">
        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">How a file is kept<span class="src">&middot; the same for every module</span></span>
            {# FIVE STATED ROWS AND A FOOT THAT SUMS THEM, which is what the
               settled design draws: the rows are the reference a reader checks
               a fact against, the foot is the whole card in one line. #}
            <div class="rln"><span>Where an original lives</span><span class="mono d">outside the web root, always</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>How it is reached</span><span class="mono acc">a request the app answers after a permission check</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Small pictures per file</span><span class="mono d">exactly one &mdash; never a set of sizes</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Small picture size</span><span class="mono d">~{{ thumbnailLongEdge }} px on the long side</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>What decides the type</span><span class="mono d">detection, never the file&rsquo;s name</span></div>
            <div class="sxfoot"><span>originals outside the site &middot; one ~{{ thumbnailLongEdge }}px picture per file &middot; type by detection &middot; a refusal reads as not found</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Limits<span class="src">&middot; typed on the target</span></span>
            <div class="rln"><span>Largest single file</span><span class="mono d">{{ maxBytes|storage_bytes }}</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Retention</span><span class="mono d">none &mdash; a file lives as long as its record</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Quota warning</span><span class="mono {{ nearQuota ? 'r' : 'w' }}">at {{ warningPercent }} % of what was bought &middot; {{ nearQuota ? 'a target has passed it' : 'no target is near it' }}</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>What happens at the quota</span><span class="mono r">the attach fails on the record&rsquo;s own page, with the reason</span></div>
            {# Quota is not in the model: it is what was bought, typed here so the bar
               above can be drawn. #}
            <p class="use">A target with no quota typed draws no bar, never a full one.</p>
            <div class="sxfoot">
                <span>Editing any of these is the configure page</span>
                <span class="sp"></span>
                <a class="tgl" href="{{ path(constant('Uhifadhi\\Storage\\Controller\\FilesConfigureController::SETTINGS')) }}">Files settings</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# THE ONE HINT THE FILES PAGES CARRY, and it is here rather than on the
       register: a reader comes to a register to find a file, and this is what
       they want after they have failed to. The words are the register's own
       lead, moved — the owner ruled on that text, pointing at it.

       ITS ONE INNER EMPHASIS DID NOT COME WITH IT. The lead carried a second
       bold on "never upload"; the shell's partial bolds the lead and escapes
       the rest, which is what keeps every hint in the product reading alike.
       The words are unchanged. #}
    {{ include('@Shell/_page_hint.html.twig', {
        lead: 'Every file belongs to a record.',
        say: 'Browse, find, check, tidy — never upload. A file arrives by being attached to a record. Originals sit outside the website and are handed over only after a permission check.',
    }) }}
{% endblock %}
